-- boi:expect-after select (select count(*) from public.news_articles where content like $p$%Updated 1 Oct 2026: MyBrickHouse's online store is now LEGO.in.%$p$) + (select count(*) from public.reviews where content like $p$%Updated 1 Oct 2026: MyBrickHouse's online store is now LEGO.in.%$p$) + (select count(*) from public.guides where content like $p$%Updated 1 Oct 2026: MyBrickHouse's online store is now LEGO.in.%$p$) + (select count(*) from public.news_articles where content like $p$%LEGO.in.in%$p$) + (select count(*) from public.guides where content like $p$%LEGO.in.in%$p$) + abs(218 - (select count(*) from public.reviews where content like $p$%Updated 2 Oct 2026: MyBrickHouse's online store is now LEGO.in.%$p$) - (select count(*) from public.guides where content like $p$%Updated 2 Oct 2026: MyBrickHouse's online store is now LEGO.in.%$p$)) + (select count(*) from public.reviews where content ~ $r$LEGO\.in\.in|LEGO\.in,?\s+(which\s+)?(operates|runs)\M|LEGO\.in\s+is\s+LEGO.s\s+only\s+certified|LEGO\.in\s*\(LEGO.s\s+only\s+certified|LEGO\.in\s+has\s+stores|LEGO\.in\s*\([^)]*\)\s*India.s\s+LEGO\s+Certified\s+Store\M|LEGO\.in\s+is\s+(India.s|an\s+official)\s+LEGO\s+Certified\s+Store|LEGO\.in,\s+a\s+LEGO\s+Certified\s+Store$r$) + (select count(*) from public.guides where content ~ $r$LEGO\.in\.in|LEGO\.in,?\s+(which\s+)?(operates|runs)\M|LEGO\.in\s+is\s+LEGO.s\s+only\s+certified|LEGO\.in\s*\(LEGO.s\s+only\s+certified|LEGO\.in\s+has\s+stores|LEGO\.in\s*\([^)]*\)\s*India.s\s+LEGO\s+Certified\s+Store\M|LEGO\.in\s+is\s+(India.s|an\s+official)\s+LEGO\s+Certified\s+Store|LEGO\.in,\s+a\s+LEGO\s+Certified\s+Store$r$) + (select count(*) from public.news_articles where content ~ $r$LEGO\.in\.in|LEGO\.in,?\s+(which\s+)?(operates|runs)\M|LEGO\.in\s+is\s+LEGO.s\s+only\s+certified|LEGO\.in\s*\(LEGO.s\s+only\s+certified|LEGO\.in\s+has\s+stores|LEGO\.in\s*\([^)]*\)\s*India.s\s+LEGO\s+Certified\s+Store\M|LEGO\.in\s+is\s+(India.s|an\s+official)\s+LEGO\s+Certified\s+Store|LEGO\.in,\s+a\s+LEGO\s+Certified\s+Store$r$) = 0
-- Correction of fix 455 (applied to production 2 Oct 2026 05:27 UTC without chat's sample review; run 36968785112).
-- Chat's rule (round 8 item 4b): news articles keep their text (only links change; none linked to MyBrickHouse);
-- evergreen pages (reviews, guides) say LEGO.in with "Updated <date>: MyBrickHouse's online store is now LEGO.in."
-- 1. News (472): bodies restored from the exact pre-455 text (all 472 recovered offline, each verified against 455's
--    recorded checksum), so staging and production get identical text; title/excerpt/SEO from the newest pre-455
--    in-database backup (production: 20261002T052725, seconds before 455).
-- 2. Evergreen (204 reviews, 14 guides): the note's date corrected to the day it landed, 2 Oct 2026.
-- 3. Four guide lines where 455 renamed the COMPANY (MyBrickHouse runs the Certified Stores; LEGO.in is its online
--    store) or broke a domain ("LEGO.in (LEGO.in.in)"). Company-sense scan of every page 455 touched (chat, 2 Oct):
--    reviews 0 hits; guides 5 hits in these 4 pages (fixed below); news 6 hits in 2 pages (restored by step 1).
--    The after-check also asserts zero company-sense phrases in reviews, guides and news.
DO $$
DECLARE
  cand record;
  chosen text;
  n int;
BEGIN
  -- Metadata (title, excerpt, SEO) from the newest in-database backup with no 455 note: production
  -- boi_backups.public__news_articles__20261002T052725 (seconds before 455); staging: its own backup of the
  -- 00:30 seed, i.e. production's pre-455 metadata. Bodies are restored below from exact text, not from here.
  FOR cand IN
    SELECT table_name FROM information_schema.tables
    WHERE table_schema = 'boi_backups' AND table_name LIKE 'public\_\_news\_articles\_\_%'
    ORDER BY table_name DESC
  LOOP
    EXECUTE format('SELECT count(*) FROM boi_backups.%I WHERE content LIKE %L', cand.table_name, '%Updated 1 Oct 2026: MyBrickHouse''s online store is now LEGO.in.%') INTO n;
    IF n = 0 THEN chosen := cand.table_name; EXIT; END IF;
  END LOOP;
  IF chosen IS NULL THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'no pre-455 news_articles backup found in boi_backups'; END IF;
  RAISE NOTICE 'news metadata from boi_backups.%', chosen;
  EXECUTE format($q$
    UPDATE public.news_articles n
       SET title = b.title, excerpt = b.excerpt, seo_title = b.seo_title, seo_description = b.seo_description
      FROM boi_backups.%I b
     WHERE b.id = n.id AND n.content LIKE %L
  $q$, chosen, '%Updated 1 Oct 2026: MyBrickHouse''s online store is now LEGO.in.%');
END $$;

-- News bodies (472): the exact pre-455 text, recovered offline and verified against 455's own recorded
-- checksums (each md5 below = 455's expect-before md5). Matched on the current (post-455) checksum.
UPDATE public.news_articles AS n SET content = v.body
  FROM (VALUES
    ('lego-ebon-hawk-your-wallet-remains-safe-for-now', '098c8ff86334e532904469f88c00406f', $b455$The Ebon Hawk is back, sort of. The ship from Knights of the Old Republic, a game many of us still fondly remember, has been recreated by builder Jonah Frost. It’s a beautiful MOC, complete with interior rooms for your custom crew. This isn't a UCS set; it's built for play, which is a nice change. You can imagine your minifigures planning their next galactic heist in there.

This build reminds us that LEGO hasn't officially released the Ebon Hawk. It's a shame, considering how iconic the ship is. Many fans would have loved an official set. But for now, we have this excellent MOC. If you're a fan of the Old Republic era, this is a build that will definitely bring back memories. We're all hoping for a new game, and maybe, just maybe, the Ebon Hawk will be in it.

No official LEGO Ebon Hawk set exists yet, so there are no Indian store prices to check. If LEGO were to release a set of this size and detail, based on similar MOCs and official large ships, expect it to land somewhere in the ₹25,000–₹40,000 range when it eventually arrives in India. That is enough for a year's worth of biryani platters for two people. MyBrickHouse and Toycra are the stores to watch for any official Star Wars releases — use code ABHINAV12 for 12% off on orders above ₹500 at Toycra. Expect a 4–6 week lag from global launch for any official set.

Verdict: WAIT. Good set, but the price will drop.

KOTOR has a new game in development. Whether it ships on any timeline that resembles a promise is a separate question. But if it does, the Ebon Hawk is the ship that will have half the planet's nostalgia receptors firing simultaneously. LEGO should have an official set ready for that moment. They almost certainly will not. The MOC will have to do — and honestly, it does it better than most official sets would, because a fan build built for love is not constrained by retail price targets.

