While this specific creation isn't something you can buy off a shelf, it does raise questions about potential future LEGO sets. Could we see official collaborations or even new themes that blend disparate LEGO universes? The success of fan builds like this often influences LEGO's direction. For now, it's a brilliant display of fan artistry, reminding us of the enduring appeal of classic LEGO themes and the boundless possibilities of the brick. It makes you wonder what other iconic characters could be given a Bionicle makeover, or vice versa. The imagination truly is the limit when it comes to LEGO.

No official Indian pricing or availability is known for this fan-made creation. If it were officially released, expect a price point comparable to other large, detailed display sets. That would be enough to cover about 15 months of a family plan on your favourite streaming service. MyBrickHouse and Toycra will be the first places to check for any official releases, though this particular build is currently only a fan creation. Use code ABHINAV12 for 12% off on orders above ₹500 at Toycra.

