    ('lego-august-2026-releases-donkey-kong-x-files-pokmon-and-mor', 'c8a1ce92c075b1009d9f3fdaf654f08c', $b455$August 2026 is shaping up to be a massive month for LEGO fans, with a packed schedule of new releases hitting shelves. From arcade classics and iconic architecture to beloved pop culture franchises, there’s something for almost everyone. Prepare your shelves, and maybe your wallet.

Leading the charge are some major theme highlights. The LEGO Ideas line is getting three highly anticipated sets: [21369](/sets/21369-the-x-files) The X-Files, 21370 E.T. the Extra-Terrestrial, and [21372](/sets/21372-la-catrina) La Catrina. If you're a fan of retro gaming, [72051](/sets/72051-donkey-kong-arcade) Donkey Kong Arcade is set to be a big draw. For art lovers, [31221](/sets/31221-gustav-klimt-the-kiss) Gustav Klimt’s The Kiss joins the Art collection, while [21067](/sets/21067-tower-bridge) Tower Bridge offers a new architectural challenge.

Pokémon fans are in for a treat with no less than three mainline LEGO Pokémon sets: [72168](/sets/72168-rayquaza) Rayquaza, [72160](/sets/72160-arcanine) Arcanine, and [72150](/sets/72150-munchlax) Munchlax. On top of that, a staggering thirteen Pokémon Smart Play sets are rolling out, including [72167](/sets/72167-charizard-vs-jolteon-ultimate-battle) Charizard vs. Jolteon Ultimate Battle and [72164](/sets/72164-training-house-with-pikachu) Training House with Pikachu. However, these Smart Play sets will only be available in the US, UK, Australia, Germany, France, and Poland.

Pop superstar Olivia Rodrigo also gets her own LEGO Editions, with four sets based on the singer, including [11507](/sets/11507-olivia-rodrigos-flower-bouquet) Olivia Rodrigo’s Flower Bouquet. This last one cleverly crosses over with the LEGO Botanicals theme. Fans in North America will also see the arrival of Ninjago, City, and Friends sets that launched elsewhere earlier in the year.

Several gift-with-purchase (GWP) offers are also lined up. Ordering 21369 The X-Files between August 1st and 10th nets you an exclusive [40896](/sets/40896-the-x-files-scullys-lab) Scully’s Lab GWP. Spending US$130 / AU$210 / £115 / €130 on Pokémon Smart Play sets between the same dates will get you [40887](/sets/40887-ditto-as-squirtle-movie-night) Ditto as Squirtle Movie Night, though this is region-limited. In the US, ordering [72153](/sets/72153-venusaur-charizard-and-blastoise) Venusaur, Charizard and Blastoise from August 1st to 10th will also include the returning [40892](/sets/40892-kanto-region-badge-collection) Kanto Region Badge Collection. Additionally, LEGO Insiders can look forward to double points on select sets.

The LEGO Donkey Kong Arcade (72051) is priced at US$199.99. Based on the USD retail price, expect an estimated import price of ₹21,400. That’s enough to buy three high-quality biryani platters for your entire family. MyBrickHouse and Toycra will be the stores to watch for availability, likely with a 4-6 week delay from the global launch. Use code ABHINAV12 for 12% off on orders above ₹500 at Toycra.

With such a diverse range of sets and promotions, August 2026 is clearly a month where LEGO is pulling out all the stops. It's a good time to be a builder, though perhaps not the best time for your bank balance.

