    ('lego-conventions-are-back-how-to-avoid-the-dreaded-con-crud', '1a6324f1c2fee1e7f567c025846cf925', $b455$The call of the convention is strong. You’ve planned your outfits, mapped out your strategy for snagging exclusive merch, and mentally prepared for the sheer volume of plastic bricks. But there's a dark side to all this brick-tastic fun: "con crud." This delightful term refers to the inevitable cold, flu, or general malaise that strikes after a weekend spent in close proximity to thousands of fellow LEGO fans. It’s the post-con blues, but with sneezes.

BrickNerd recently dropped a guide on how to navigate these germ-filled gatherings. It’s not exactly a LEGO set review, but honestly, some of us treat our health like a rare minifigure — easily misplaced. The article covers the usual suspects: hand sanitizer is your best friend, avoid touching your face like it’s a forbidden build instruction, and for goodness sake, wash your hands. Basic stuff, right? Yet, how many of us actually follow it religiously when a rare MOC is just a few feet away?

Beyond the immediate germ warfare, the guide also touches on the mental toll. The post-convention slump is real. You’ve spent days immersed in a world of pure plastic joy, and now you’re back to reality. Suddenly, your office feels drab, and your commute is a lot less exciting than a LEGO Ideas reveal. It's like finishing an epic build and staring at an empty display shelf.

The advice boils down to preparation and recovery. Pack your vitamins, get enough sleep (if that’s even possible at a convention), and stay hydrated. After the event, give yourself time to decompress. Don't immediately dive back into a 10,000-piece build if you're feeling drained. Maybe a smaller, simpler set? Or just a good cup of chai and some quiet time.

While there's no specific LEGO set to price check here, the cost of attending a major LEGO convention can add up. Consider travel, accommodation, and any exclusive items you might be tempted by. If you're eyeing a trip to a big event, factor in potential medical costs if you do catch that infamous con crud. For those looking to pick up some new bricks after the con, MyBrickHouse and Toycra are your go-to spots. Use code ABHINAV12 for 12% off on orders above ₹500 at Toycra. This advice is more about safeguarding your investment in fun, and frankly, avoiding a week of sniffles is priceless.

