Even with strict constraints, like gonkos_legocreations' challenge of only seven elements and one color, builders are creating ideal little guys. Alex Lyman is mixing it up with printed elements from Friends, Dots, and more, even building a fish-adjacent character inspired by a sticker. Trolley_hoarse found the absolute smallest guy, while farawaybricks has assembled a whole team of bipeds and oozes.

L.A.Miranda, known for her LEGO dolls, crafted a little guy with ice cream cone thighs that somehow work as fishnets. Blasted_blockz introduced us to RODAGONUS, DEVOURER OF LIVERS (who also plays the lute!), proving "little guy" can also mean rich lore. Chloe Staszewska repurposed the Woodstock hair piece for a tiny beard, and Bamboo Bricks reminds us that "little guy" is about energy, not piece count.

These little guys are weird, mostly harmless, and can be any gender. Brickbytes even recreated Pingu, the claymation star. Dissolved Frog's little crab looks like magic from just a few parts. m1ndxbend3r even proved Batman can be a quintessential little guy. And of course, Ivy herself submitted one.

At the end of the month, Ivybrickss will select three favorites to win a brick-built trophy. So, if you have some bricks lying around, consider joining the fun.

