The builder behind this creation is Dulce Gomez, a Mexican designer who poured her personal connection to the iconic figure into the submission. She explains that La Catrina, often depicted as an elegantly dressed skeleton, is a symbol of Mexican identity and a commentary on social class from early 20th-century Mexico. It’s a reminder that death is a natural part of life, and that even in mortality, there’s room for art and satire. Gomez's passion for the project shines through, highlighting how LEGO can be a powerful medium for cultural expression and education.

While we don’t have specific set numbers or pricing details for India yet, the anticipation for this set is already building. The LEGO Ideas line often produces unique and display-worthy models, and La Catrina promises to be no exception. It’s a chance for fans to own a piece of art that represents a significant cultural symbol, crafted with the familiar precision and charm of LEGO. We’re expecting this to be a conversation starter on any display shelf.

